            ('Why are no results shown yet?', 'Because none have been recorded to the standard set out above, and we do not publish examples made up to fill a page.\nWhen a month has been gathered for a trade and city, it is shown here with its date and the sources cited.'),
            ('Can a business pay to be recommended by an assistant?', 'No. A place in an assistant’s answer cannot be bought, from us or from anyone. Some assistants show advertisements, which are labeled.\nWhat can be paid for is the work that makes a business readable, confirmed and chosen. That work is slower, and it lasts.'),
            ('Why do the answers change from one chat to the next?', 'Because an assistant composes each answer afresh, from searches that may return different pages. Names near the edge come and go.\nA business named in all three runs is firmly placed. One named once in three is not. That is why the Index asks three times.'),
            ('Do all assistants name the same businesses?', 'Often not. Each draws on different search indexes and listings, so ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity can give three different lists.\nThat is why the Index asks several assistants, and why the work has to cover more than one. Checking a single assistant tells you little.'),
            ('Will you name my competitors in the Index?', 'The Index records what the assistants say in public answers, which anyone can obtain by asking the same question.\nNo client of ours is identified as a client, and no private data is used or shown. It is a record of public answers, nothing more.'),
